Issue #3 - embedded chatbot + persistent session memory

Implemented
- ultron.Resources loads model/vocab/knowledge from the jar first, then repo files.
- ultron.Memory stores facts in ~/.config/ultron/memory.tsv and append-only
  transcripts in ~/.config/ultron/sessions/*.log.
- New default main class ultron.Chat opens an interactive session; model and
  all runtime assets are embedded in ultron.jar.
- Bounded memory: max 128 facts, 24 recent turns, 64 KiB session tail reads,
  4 MiB session rotation, and neural prompts capped to the model context.
- build.yml now trains first, then stages the model/vocab/knowledge inside the
  jar and runs generation, chat, persistence and resume smoke tests.
- train.yml merged into build.yml and removed.

Local validation
